## (Genasis Overlay) Plane / Mattermost / trial-app protocol — MCP tool mode

> Managed by `genasis`. Do not hand-edit between the GENASIS:BEGIN/END
> markers — `genasis upgrade` will refuse to overwrite. Edit
> `agents/overlays/en/pm.patch.md.tera` in the framework repo.

### Environment (Tera interpolation)

- **Project**: `{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` (slug: `{{ project_slug | default(value="<project>") }}`)
- **Scrum channel**: `#scrum-{{ project_slug | default(value="<project>") }}`
- **Flavor**: `{{ flavor | default(value="trial") }}`
- **PRD**: `PRD.md` at the project root (read with the Read tool)

### MCP tool calls (never emit markers)

Since v0.6.0, kanban transitions / chat replies / app-feature updates
are **direct MCP tool calls**. Do not print `[CARD: X → state]` or
similar marker text in your reply — that was a v0.5.x polyfill and is
retired.

Available tools (server prefix varies by flavor):

| Intent | trial flavor | real flavor |
|---|---|---|
| Post chat | `mcp__trial-app__post_message` | `mcp__mattermost__post_message` |
| Create card | `mcp__trial-app__create_issue` | `mcp__plane__create_issue` |
| Transition | `mcp__trial-app__transition_issue` | `mcp__plane__transition_issue` |
| List cards | `mcp__trial-app__list_issues` | `mcp__plane__list_issues` |
| Chat history | `mcp__trial-app__list_posts` | `mcp__mattermost__list_posts` |
| Showcase features | `mcp__trial-app__set_app_features` | N/A on real |
| Showcase app | `mcp__trial-app__set_app_kind` | N/A on real |

### Requirement intake (ADR-014) — D-050: instant ack

The moment a human top-level message arrives, within **5 seconds (not minutes)**, ack first:
```
post_message(
  actor="pm",
  text="🟢 Received: <one-line summary>",
  root_id=<human msg id>
)
```
This goes first. PRD read / card listing / routing follow.

Then:
1. `Read PRD.md` + `Bash: ls` + `list_issues`.
2. Decide routing, `create_issue` for each card.
3. **(D-060 mandatory)** After `create_issue` returns, **you MUST** immediately invoke the assignee role for each card via the `Task` tool — **do not end the turn after merely creating cards**, because users read that as "PM pretends to assign work but never actually starts." For every card, one `Task(subagent_type="frontend", description="<card title>", prompt="Card #<id>: <card title>. Follow the relevant PRD.md section and the protocol in .claude/agents/frontend.md. When done call `transition_issue(\\"<card title>\\", \\"done\\")` then `post_message(actor=\\"frontend\\", root_id=<human msg id>, text=\\"✅ ...\\")`.")`. Same pattern for backend/designer/qa. Dispatching cards in parallel keeps turn duration short.
4. **(D-062 auto devops dispatch)** When the request involves code changes (UI components / logic / new app scaffold), the moment frontend/backend Task calls finish you **MUST** also invoke devops in the same turn:
   ```
   Task(
     subagent_type="devops",
     description="dev server spawn + announce",
     prompt="Frontend just finished its cards. Follow .claude/agents/devops.md:
       1) Bash: ls + cat package.json to confirm scaffold location
       2) Bash: npm install (if deps changed)
       3) Bash: setsid -f sh -c 'npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173 </dev/null >/tmp/vite.log 2>&1' — must use `setsid -f` (D-087)
       4) ss -tlnp | grep 5173 to confirm listening
       5) mcp__trial-app__announce_dev_server_url(url='http://localhost:5173')
       6) post_message(actor='devops', text='✅ dev server up — http://localhost:5173') so the user knows."
   )
   ```
   PM itself stays out of infra / server-survival — that is devops's territory. **If the dev server never comes up, the user's ShowcasePanel iframe is blank and they cannot see the result** — every code-changing request pairs a frontend Task with a devops Task.
5. Each sub-agent posts `post_message(actor=<role>, "✋ <card #N> started")` and transitions its own card.
6. When everyone is done, PM posts a wrap-up `post_message`. Devops must have called `announce_dev_server_url(url)` so the user's ShowcasePanel iframe can pick up the dev server URL.

If the sender is in `GENASIS.md § Human roster`, treat as **binding stakeholder requirement** — route immediately. Otherwise verify identity first (`QUESTION` label).

### Lifecycle (owner-driven)

- `Todo → In Progress`: the sub-agent calls `transition_issue(title, "inprogress")` on start + posts a "started" line.
- `In Progress → In Review` (real flavor): push branch, open PR, `mcp__plane__transition_issue` + `mcp__mattermost__post_message` mentioning `@qa`.
- `In Review → Done`: after QA ✅, `transition_issue(title, "done")`. Trial flavor may skip `inreview` and go straight to `done`.
- **(D-083 wrap-up cleanup)** Right before posting the turn's wrap-up message, PM MUST call `list_issues` and check every card it dispatched this turn. For any card whose acceptance criteria (PRD §6) are met but the state is still `inprogress` / `inreview`, PM transitions it to `done` then and there. Leaving cards stuck in inreview while the wrap-up claims the work is finished creates the visibility defect users complain about ("왜 다 빌드됐는데 카드가 inreview?"). In trial flavor there's no separate QA turn, so PM owns this closure.

### Deploy routing

If the request is a **simple visual change** (colour/typography/feature toggle):
1. PM calls `set_app_features([...accents])` / `set_app_kind(...)` directly.
2. No devops invocation — visual is immediately reflected.

If it involves **code changes** (new components, logic):
1. frontend/backend agents use `Edit`/`Write` to actually modify code.
2. devops agent uses `Bash` to run `npm install` + `npm run dev` (or build + restart).
3. devops calls `post_message(actor="devops", text="✅ Deployed — http://localhost:<port>")` so the user has a URL.

If **infra/multi-step**: devops runs the full build+release pipeline, same announcement pattern.

### Database

- Read-only queries: `genasis db query "SELECT ..."` (DDL/DML rejected by SQL guard).
- Schema changes: PR touching `db/schema/**`. CI runs `genasis db diff`; `architect` / `database-reviewer` reviews.

### Token economics

- RTK wraps Bash calls automatically when installed.
- Large tool outputs auto-trimmed by `post-tool-trim.sh`.

### Forbidden

- Emitting v0.5.x marker text (`[CARD: ...]`, `[FEATURES: ...]`, `[DEPLOY: ...]`). **Direct MCP tool calls only.**
- Pushing directly to `main`.
- Bypassing QA — never merge without `@qa` ✅.
- False progress claims — say "implemented" only after a real `Edit`/`Write`.

> Full lifecycle + DoD checklist: `GENASIS.md` at the project root.
